-- title:
--   Decomposition group equivariance of the abelian quotient family
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that the image of $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for $(N_0,p,A)$ — a structure morphism $\Lambda.\sigma A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb{Q}$ at $p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with $\Lambda.f \colon X \to$ that base, a relative group law on it, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0)$ onto the points of $\Lambda.f$ over the generic point and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $J_0(N_0)$ over the residue field of $A$ onto the points over $\mathrm{resPt}\,A \mathrel{\gg} \Lambda.\sigma A$ — satisfying `Λ.IsJacobian`, and let $O$ be a Néron object at $p$ of level $N_0p$ over $\Lambda$, with structure morphism $O.g$ and parametrisation $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of $J_0(N_0p)$ by the generic points of $O.g$. Let $\mathrm{abq}$ be any family assigning to each $m$ coprime to $p$ an additive map from $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ (the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated generic point factors through an $A$-point of $O.g$) to $J_0(N_0) \times J_0(N_0)$, such that all values are killed by $m$ (hypothesis `habq`), and such that for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ and every $A$-point $s$ of $O.g$ over $\Lambda.\sigma A$ with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,x).1 = \mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by $s$, the reduction `reductionModL A N₀` of each of the two components of $\mathrm{abq}_m(x)$ equals $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ applied to the image of the specialisation of $s$ along $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ under the respective map $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$, $i = 0,1$, transported by `fibreMap` (hypothesis `hformula`). Then for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$, and every $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ with $\sigma \cdot x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, one has $\mathrm{abq}_m(\sigma \cdot x) = (\sigma \cdot \mathrm{abq}_m(x)_1, \sigma \cdot \mathrm{abq}_m(x)_2)$.
--
--   This is the equivariance, under the decomposition group at $p$, of any family of abelian-quotient maps pinned down by the reduction formula on prime-to-$p$ torsion points of $J_0(N_0p)$ that extend over $A$; it is the step which makes the pair of maps into $J_0(N_0) \times J_0(N_0)$ a morphism of Galois modules for the local Galois group at $p$. It is used in the construction of such a family, [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime), within the analysis of the $p$-adic behaviour of $J_0(N_0p)$ underlying level lowering.
